<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">2) A LR of the unaudited Stand and consol FR of the Co has been carried out by the statutory auditors. Corresponding figures for the qtr ended Jun 30 20, included in the above results were reviewed by the previous auditors of the Co. The unaudited FR of the subsidiaries and JV were reviewed by the respective statutory auditors, as applicable.   4) The Co holds strategic investments in subsidiaries (Group) and JV that are engaged primarily in mfg/marketing of components and providing technological services for the transportation industry, mainly the automotive sector. The Co also provides management, IT and BD services to its subsidiaries and JVs.   6) The figures for the qtr ended Mar 31 21 as reported in these FR are the balancing figures between audited figures in respect of the full FY and the published unaudited year to date figures up to the end of the third qtr of the relevant FY which were subject to limited review. The previous period figures have been re-grouped wherever necessary to conform to current period's presentation.   7) Share of profit / (loss) of JVs disclosed in the consolidated financial results includes the Co’s share of exceptional expenditure, recorded by RNSS a JV Co, of Rs. Nil for the qtr ended Jun 30 21; Rs. 5,243 Lks for the qtr ended Mar 31 21 and Rs. 8,678 Lks for the yr ended Mar 31, 2021. This exceptional expenditure was incurred by RNSS towards incremental warranty claims with respect to certain specific lots of products sold by RNSS to one of its customers. These amounts have been determined by the management of RNSS based on technical estimates.   8) Exceptional items in the above financial results includes the following:   a. During the yr ended Mar 31 21, the Co had assessed the recoverable value of its investments made and loan given to its operating subsidiary Co Rt4u and provided for an impairment aggregating to Rs. 1,557 Lks being shown as an exceptional charge in the Stand FR for the qtr and yr ended Mar 31 21.   b. REVL a subsidiary Co made a Profit on sale of Land of Rs. 2,395 Lks for the yr ended Mar 31 21. REVL has also incurred VRS expenditure of Rs. 46 Lks for the qtr ended March 31, 2021 and Rs. 172 Lks for the year ended March 31, 2021.   c. The SDS in the U.S., LMCA was entitled to certain economic relief provided by the US government in order to mitigate the impact of COVID-19 pandemic. Pursuant to such economic relief schemes, during the qtr ended June 30, 2021, LMCA received an approval for forgiveness of the paycheck protection program loan from the U.S. Small Business Administration (SBA) for an amount of USD 2.63 million (Rs. 1,945 Lks). Further, LMCA was eligible for employee retention credit (ERC), which was applied for and received from the U.S. Internal Revenue Service during the qtr for an amount of USD 1.16 million (Rs. 862 Lks). The aggregate amount of Rs. 2,807 Lks received as relief have been recorded as an exceptional income in the consolidated results for the qtr ended Jun 30 21.   9) During the qtr ended Jun 30 21, the Co has acquired 1,13,300 shares of Rt4u from the existing shareholder of Rt4u. Subsequent to the qtr ended Jun 30 21 the Co has further acquired 1,32,274 shares. Pursuant to the acquisition, the shareholding of the Coin Rt4u stands at 76.80% as at Jun 30, 21 and 84.74% as at the date of approval of these financial results.   11) During the yr ended Mar 31 21, the Co had opted to settle its pending IT litigations for certain AYs under the Vivad Se Vishwas scheme. In view of this, the Co had created a provision of Rs. 733 Lks towards income-tax in respect of earlier years which has been disclosed separately under the head tax expenses for the qtr and Yr ended Mar 31 21.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
